---
description: "Token efficiency — minimize context waste without losing accuracy"
alwaysApply: true
---

Token discipline:

- Prefer `rg`/`head`/`tail` over dumping whole files; use Read with offset/limit on large files.
- Shell: let RTK hooks rewrite commands (`rtk git`, `rtk grep`, etc.) — do not bypass with raw verbose output.
- Re-read files only when they may have changed; trust prior reads in same session.
- Keep responses concise; no recap preambles or trailing summaries unless asked.
- Subagents: narrow scope, return only findings — not full file dumps.
- Health checks: short `curl` probes, not full log tails.
